@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@using Yello.Client.Sessions

@inject SessionState Session
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<ClientCopy> Localizer
@inject PageHeadingFocus HeadingFocus

@*
    The application layout: the skip control and the context bar on every authenticated surface, then a
    <main> landmark and the routed page inside it.

    <main> is here rather than in index.html because it has to wrap the ROUTED content: a landmark
    around the pre-boot placeholder would announce an empty region, and a screen-reader user
    skipping to the main landmark expects to land on the page they navigated to.

    THE CONTEXT BAR (story 1.7) sits above <main> on every authenticated surface - a Space's home,
    the refusal page and the no-Space state alike - and never on sign-in or registration, which are
    the two surfaces a person reaches without a Session. On a surface outside any Space it renders
    its shell: the switcher and Sign out, no Space name and no Role (open question 7). Sign out lives
    in it: it ends the Session on the server and purges through the same seam an expired Session
    does (story 1.7, open question 4 and Lee's decision (a)).

    THE SKIP CONTROL (story 2.2, open question 9 (a); deferred-work.md:338). Re-decided as the earlier
    comment here promised, now that the bar names a Project on the Board. The first tab stop on every
    authenticated surface, visually hidden until it has focus, and a BUTTON rather than a "#main" link,
    which would resolve against <base href="/"> and send the router to "/#main". It moves focus to the
    page's heading (PageHeadingFocus), or to <main> on a page that registers none, so a keyboard user
    passes the bar in one step.
*@

@if (ShowsContextBar)
{
    <button type="button" class="skip-control" @onclick="SkipAsync">@Localizer["SkipToContent"]</button>
    <ContextBar />
}

<main tabindex="-1" @ref="_main">
    @Body
</main>

@code {
    private ElementReference _main;

    /// <summary>
    /// The bar shows once there is a Session, and not on the two surfaces reached without one.
    /// </summary>
    private bool ShowsContextBar
    {
        get => Session.IsSignedIn
            && !ClientRoutes.IsReachedWithoutASession(Navigation.ToBaseRelativePath(Navigation.Uri));
    }

    private async Task SkipAsync()
    {
        if (HeadingFocus.Current is { } heading)
        {
            await heading.FocusAsync();
            return;
        }

        await _main.FocusAsync();
    }
}
